  "DEVELOPMENT_LEADS": [
    {
      "id": "SCP-01",
      "shortcoming": "Fixed 24-bit dimension",
      "detail": "The Hodge Conjecture applies to varieties of ALL complex dimensions. UBP is locked to 24-bit vectors via the Golay code. This is the single most limiting factor for applying UBP to algebraic geometry.",
      "development_lead": "Build a parameterized code family: extend Golay to BCH codes [2^m - 1, k, d] for arbitrary m, or develop a 'dimension-adaptive' lattice system. The Barnes-Wall ladder (16D \u2192 64D \u2192 256D) is a starting point but needs full TGIC integration.",
      "priority": "CRITICAL"
    },
    {
      "id": "SCP-02",
      "shortcoming": "No complex structure (GF(2) only)",
      "detail": "Hodge theory is fundamentally about the complex structure on cohomology: H^k(X,C) = \u2295 H^{p,q} where p+q=k. The UBP works over GF(2), which has no notion of complex conjugation, holomorphic forms, or the Hodge star.",
      "development_lead": "Implement a GF(4) or GF(p) extension of the TGIC engine. GF(4) (F_4) is the smallest field extension of GF(2) and introduces a complex-conjugation analog (Frobenius automorphism). This would allow modeling h^{p,q} vs h^{q,p} as genuinely distinct rather than symmetric-by-construction.",
      "priority": "CRITICAL"
    },
    {
      "id": "SCP-03",
      "shortcoming": "Syndrome=0 \u2194 Codeword is tautological",
      "detail": "In the UBP, being a codeword (syndrome=0) is DEFINITIONALLY equivalent to being 'rational/algebraic'. There is no analog of a class that is Hodge (i.e., type (p,p)) but NOT algebraic. This is exactly what the Hodge Conjecture's counterexamples are about.",
      "development_lead": "Introduce a 'Hodge filtration' within the UBP that is STRICTLY WEAKER than codeword membership. E.g., vectors whose syndrome has weight \u2264 k (not just 0) could model 'Hodge but possibly transcendental' classes. The threshold k would parameterize the 'gap' between Hodge and algebraic \u2014 the very thing the conjecture is about.",
      "priority": "HIGH"
    },
    {
      "id": "SCP-04",
      "shortcoming": "No intersection product",
      "detail": "Algebraic cycles intersect (cup product in cohomology). The Hodge Conjecture requires that the ring structure of algebraic cycles maps onto the ring structure of Hodge classes. UBP has no multiplication of cohomology classes.",
      "development_lead": "Implement a cohomology ring product for the Golay code space. Natural candidate: the AND operation on 24-bit vectors models intersection (cap product). The TGIC's rune_resonance_xy already uses AND \u2014 formalize this as an intersection product and study its ring-theoretic properties (associative? commutative? unital?).",
      "priority": "HIGH"
    },
    {
      "id": "SCP-05",
      "shortcoming": "Only 2-torsion visible",
      "detail": "Hodge counterexamples (Atiyah-Hitchin, Kuga-Satake) often involve torsion classes of odd order. GF(2) can only model 2-torsion, missing the most interesting counterexamples.",
      "development_lead": "Extend the substrate to GF(p) for small primes p = 3, 5, 7. A 'multi-prime substrate' running several GF(p) instances in parallel and comparing results via Chinese Remainder Theorem could detect torsion phenomena invisible to GF(2).",
      "priority": "MEDIUM"
    },
    {
      "id": "SCP-06",
      "shortcoming": "No projective variety model",
      "detail": "The Hodge Conjecture is stated for smooth projective varieties. UBP has no notion of a variety, its defining equations, or its embedding in projective space.",
      "development_lead": "Develop a 'binary projective geometry' layer: define binary analogs of P^n, homogeneous coordinates, and the Veronese embedding. The Golay code's 4096 codewords could be interpreted as 'points' in a binary projective space of dimension 11 (P^11 has 2^12 - 1 = 4095 nonzero vectors mod scaling \u2248 4096).",
      "priority": "MEDIUM"
    },
    {
      "id": "SCP-07",
      "shortcoming": "NRCI is a scalar, not a grading",
      "detail": "Hodge structure is a GRADED decomposition H^k = \u2295 H^{p,q}. NRCI reduces everything to a single scalar, losing the grading information that is essential to even stating the Hodge Conjecture.",
      "development_lead": "Replace scalar NRCI with a 'Hodge NRCI vector' \u2014 a matrix or graded tensor that preserves (p,q)-type information. The 3-block structure (X, Y, Z each 8-bit) is a natural starting point: define NRCI^{p,q} for each block-pair combination.",
      "priority": "HIGH"
    },
    {
      "id": "SCP-08",
      "shortcoming": "No Leray spectral sequence or mixed Hodge theory",
      "detail": "Modern approaches to Hodge use spectral sequences, mixed Hodge structures (Deligne), and category-theoretic methods. UBP has none of these.",
      "development_lead": "Implement a 'binary spectral sequence': a sequence of NRCI computations at increasing 'resolution' (analogous to the E_r pages). The Barnes-Wall lattice ladder (16\u219264\u2192256) provides a natural resolution scale. This would enable studying degenerations and limits \u2014 key tools in Hodge theory.",
      "priority": "LOW"
    }
  ],
